WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:04.889
A clock has two hands. The short hand shows the hour.

00:05.339 --> 00:11.590
The long hand shows the minutes. When it points straight up at the twelve, it is o'clock.

00:11.590 --> 00:13.698
This clock says three o'clock.

00:14.148 --> 00:20.918
When the long hand points straight down at the six, it is half past. That is thirty minutes.

00:20.918 --> 00:23.273
This clock says half past three.

00:23.723 --> 00:29.679
Each number stands for five minutes. Count by fives to the three. Five, ten,

00:29.679 --> 00:33.127
fifteen. This clock says quarter past three.

00:33.577 --> 00:40.683
To tell time, look at the short hand for the hour first. Then look at the long hand for the minutes.
